From d1bafc98aea455e84909b9a7390a1b5533f5f14c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:43:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 117/117] DOS-PORT: patch 0117 -- don't build the light table
 when nothing can darken

create_light_table() costs 1351 ms on Trilby's Notes and 4699 ms on
BENCH8 (HW-486-66, patch 0109's brackets): 65,280 bestfit_color() calls,
each a palette scan. It ran on every load_new_room(), because ac/room.cpp
nulls color_map immediately before calling generate_light_table() and so
defeats that function's own guard.

Patch 0114's counters showed the table is usually never read at all. Over
Trilby's entire 5000-tick benchmark on real hardware:
"colormap_consumers transblend=0 litblend=0". The engine computed it and
never looked at it.

SAFETY IS THE LOAD-BEARING PART, not the optimisation, and it is built
first for that reason. Once "never built" is the common case, every
consumer path becomes one that has never executed in testing -- and our
correctness gate is DOSBox-X, which is structurally blind to a missed
hook because the path will not execute there either. A miss is also not a
glitch: libsrc/allegro/src/c/cspr.h:545 dereferences color_map BEFORE the
pixel loop, so it faults even where the blit would have drawn nothing.
So color_map is never left null once this has run: it points either at a
real table or at an identity table whose data[light][colour] = colour.
A missed hook renders one blend unblended instead of crashing.

Three cases:
  - room declares no darkening: table never built (the common case, and
    Gate 1's);
  - room declares darkening: built eagerly at load exactly as before, so
    no mid-game hitch is introduced for a game that uses it;
  - a script enables darkening later: the lazy hook builds it on the
    first blend.

"Declares darkening" is only a negative light level: 8-bit cannot tint or
lighten (ac/draw.cpp:1737-1748, whose own comment says so), so no tint
test is needed. Both sources are checked -- a region's Light and the
ambient play.rtint_light.

Hooked at Bitmap::TransBlendBlt AND Bitmap::LitBlendBlt, the only two
routes from AGS into Allegro's 8-bit blenders. Both, not just the lit one:
Engine/ac/draw.cpp:1447 reaches the trans path on
"src_has_alpha && alpha == 0xFF" with no colour-depth test. The hook is a
function pointer installed by the Engine, because Common/ must not depend
on Engine/ where the table and palette state live.

Retains patch 0113's reuse cache for the case where the table IS needed,
keyed on the palette AND rgb_map's state, since rgb_map non-null selects a
different branch in create_light_table() and yields a different table from
the same palette.
